  "pull_request": {
    "number": 228,
    "title": "Implement confidence-based default lint severities",
    "body": "## close #101 \r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR aligns the linter's default severity levels with the confidence-and-impact model defined in `roadmap_mvp.md`.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n### Lint Defaults\r\n\r\n- Updated lint declarations to reflect their documented confidence/impact classification.\r\n- High-confidence, high-impact lint(s) now default to **Deny**.\r\n- Context-dependent lint(s) continue to default to **Warn**.\r\n- No lint detection logic was modified.\r\n\r\n### Configuration\r\n\r\n- Verified that user-defined severity levels in `budget.toml` continue to override the default lint levels.\r\n- Added regression coverage for override behaviour.\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n\r\nUpdated:\r\n\r\n- `docs/lints/README.md`\r\n- `README.md`\r\n\r\nDocumentation now reflects:\r\n- current default severities\r\n- confidence/impact classification\r\n- override behaviour\r\n- rationale for default levels\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\nAdded/updated tests covering:\r\n\r\n- Deny-by-default diagnostics\r\n- Warn-by-default diagnostics\r\n- `budget.toml` override behaviour\r\n- Correct emitted diagnostic levels\r\n\r\n## Breaking Change\r\n\r\nChanging the default severity of a lint may cause existing CI pipelines to fail where they previously emitted warnings only. Users can continue to override defaults through `budget.toml`. This change may warrant a version bump depending on the project's release policy.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- ✅ `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\r\n- ✅ `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\r\n- ✅ `cargo test --workspace`\r\n\r\nCloses #<issue-number>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Local Test Output\r\n\r\nPaste the full output of:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\r\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings\r\ncargo test --workspace\r\n```\r\n\r\nbefore submitting the PR.",
